.TH GIT-CITY 1 "" "git-city" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
git-city \- turn a git history into an animated 3D city
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git city
[\fIbuild\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B git city init
[\fB\-\-shared\fR]
.br
.B git city serve
[\fIdir\fR] [\fB\-\-port\fR \fIn\fR] [\fB\-\-open\fR]
.br
.B git city audit
[\fIdir\fR]
.br
.B git city cache
\fBstatus\fR|\fBclear\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
git-city reads a repository's history and writes a static site with an animated 3D city: each file is a building, each
folder a district, each contributor a block of time. Names are hidden unless a config rule reveals them.
.PP
Each command also runs as \fBgit city\fR, which is how git finds it.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B build
Build the site (the default command). Resumes from the cache when it can.
.TP
.B init [--shared]
Write a commented starter config. By default it is the personal config under the git directory, which is never
committed. \fB\-\-shared\fR writes \fIgit-city.config.jsonc\fR at the repository root, to be committed. It lists the
detected Modules, External Dependencies and Themes, and refuses to overwrite an existing config.
.TP
.B serve [dir]
Serve a built site on localhost only. Without \fB\-\-port\fR it uses the first free port from 4173 up. The world file
is never cached.
.TP
.B audit [dir]
List every string in a built site, one per line, as id and text.
.TP
.B cache status|clear
Inspect or remove the build cache in \fI.git/git-city/\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-C " path"
Run as if started in \fIpath\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-branch " name"
Read this branch instead of the default branch.
.TP
.BI \-\-out " dir"
Output folder (default \fIgit-city-site/\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-config " path"
Read this config file instead of the shared and personal configs.
.TP
.B \-\-strict
Fail the build on near-miss names (exit code 2).
.TP
.B \-\-private
Ignore every reveal in the config.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " name"
The Theme for names and colours: \fImodern\fR or \fImedieval\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-seed " text"
The seed for Generated names; overrides \fInaming.seed\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-fresh
Rebuild the cache from scratch.
.TP
.B \-\-wait
Wait for another running build instead of failing.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the build result as JSON on standard output.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Print nothing on success. Warnings and errors are still shown.
.TP
.BI \-\-port " n"
Port for \fBserve\fR, used exactly.
.TP
.B \-\-open
Open the served site in the browser (\fBserve\fR).
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Show the version.
.PP
Flags only make the output more private. When a flag and the config set the same thing, the flag wins.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, possibly with warnings.
.TP
.B 1
Error.
.TP
.B 2
The privacy check failed.
.TP
.B 3
Another run holds the lock (use \fB\-\-wait\fR to wait for it).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I git-city.config.jsonc
Shared config at the repository root, committed.
.TP
.I .git/git-city/config.jsonc
Personal config, never committed. Its rules come last.
.TP
.I .git/git-city/
Build cache.
.SH SEE ALSO
git(1)
